  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas is initially at temperature T and Volume V. Its volume increases by <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> due to an increase in temperature <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>,</mo></math> (P remains constant). The quantity <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">δ</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> varies with temperature as"
